blocks.en:
Concerning span-level evaluation, we report F1-exact, F1-partial, and F1-token metrics for both AL and Target spans identification:
F1-exact requires identical predicted and gold span boundaries;
F1-partial credits a prediction when it overlaps the gold span;
F1-token is the binary macro-F1 over tokens..
We report median scores and standard deviation over three training runs.
Concerning significance tests, we apply similar tests as for sentence-level evaluation: the significance test at 5% on the median run.

blocks.zh:
关于跨度评价,我们报告用于AL和目标的F1-精确度、F1-部分度和F1-托克度量标准跨度:
F1-精确度要求相同的预测和黄金边界;
F1-部分分值为与黄金相重叠的预测;
F1-token是二进制宏-F1 大于符.
我们报告三次训练的中位分和标准偏差。
关于意义测试,我们采用与判刑级评估类似的测试:在中值运行时,意义测试为5%。

blocks.en:
Future work. Three priority directions emerge:
(1) enriching existing corpora with complete ALI annotations to build structured benchmarks;
(2) integrating target–AL linking and exploring multi-task architectures exploiting the hierarchical taxonomy;
(3) systematic bias evaluation, as ALI enables fine-grained error analysis at the token level unlike the ALC task.

blocks.zh:
未来工作。 出现了三个优先方向:
(1) 以完整的ALI说明来充实现有的公司,以建立结构化的基准;
(2) 整合目标-AL连接和探索利用分级分类的多任务结构;
(3) 系统性的偏差评价,因为与ALC任务不同,ALI在符号层面能够进行精细的误差分析.
